WEBVTT

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.500
Not going so we can die

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:14.590
We were in a flurry of activity preparing for departure.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.660
The space ship's course calculations...

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.130
...testing and adjusting the gravity control system...

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.490
Increasing output 10%!

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:36.380
...inspecting and tuning the various systems in the cockpit...

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.060
...with Survive translating the language of this planet for us.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.170
What are you doing here in the dark?

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.040
I was just thinking how pretty it is.

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:12.940
The stars...

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.550
We're finally leaving tomorrow.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:26.760
Is it okay to let me pilot the ship?

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:28.350
Kaoru...

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.140
Even just now, you were inspecting everything again yourself, weren't you?

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.270
Because everyone's lives are in my hands.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.110
I believe in you, Kaoru.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.540
What I told you before about Louis...

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:59.100
...I think Louis did say, "Live!" back then.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:00.230
I thought so.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:06.080
The situation was much like when I was saved by my dad.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.430
However painful things may be...

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.560
...or however tough, don't give up.

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:19.090
Live until the end.

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.110
Live...

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:24.860
Daddy!

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.490
Live!

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:35.180
Ever since then, it's as though the word 'live' has been etched into my heart.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:39.850
Whenever I'm in danger, that word always comes to mind.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.360
I feel like I was saved by that word as well.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.230
Kaoru...

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:13.950
Bravo!

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.410
But I'm sure none but I, who once aimed to be a pianist,

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:20.420
can appreciate the greatness of your performance, Menori.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.390
That's news to me.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.850
Everyone says you were made to play the piano and got frustrated with it.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:28.010
Shut up.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.010
So what did you come all the way out here to do?

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:37.460
You seemed anxious about tomorrow, so I came to cheer you up.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.890
Aren't <i>you</i> the one who's nervous?

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.900
What are you saying? I was worried about you, Menori!

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:46.880
Unfortunately...

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.300
...I've had a wonderful gentleman here to encourage me for quite some time.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.060
Good evening!

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:57.650
Oh, just Adam.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:04.870
So many things have happened since we came to this planet.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:06.910
It's true.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:11.920
Stop!

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.460
I hate you, Bell!

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:17.090
Sharla!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.300
I want to be of some use to Luna!

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.670
You've gotten stronger since we came to this planet, Sharla.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.100
I'm still just a spoiled child.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:30.490
That's not true.

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:32.290
Thanks.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:33.550
It's thanks to you, Bell.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:38.290
In hard times and sad times...

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:43.190
...I'm happy you were there to kindly watch over me, Bell.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.190
Sharla...

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.480
And you scolded me when I was selfish.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:53.660
It wasn't just me.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:55.820
I mean, Luna...

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:58.880
It's thanks to everyone...

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:01.410
...that I am who I am now.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:04.580
Me too, I guess.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.560
Do mine over too!

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:07.660
Mine too!

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:10.580
You're your own person!

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.060
Our parents have nothing to do with it!

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.130
This is our problem!

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:26.630
I was withdrawn and had no confidence in myself...

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:31.630
...but thanks to living here, I've been able to get my confidence back a little.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:33.560
Bell...

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:37.280
It really is thanks to everyone.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:42.450
Sharla!

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:46.350
Luna!

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:47.480
Kaoru!

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:52.400
Imagine finding you in a place like this!

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:54.530
What a coincidence!

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:56.860
It really is!

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.530
Oh, all of you came as well?

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:02.030
So what were you doing?

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.870
We were simply drawn to this beautiful starry sky!

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:09.260
Wow, you're quite the romantic.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.390
Hey!

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:12.860
Everyone!

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.010
Fancy meeting you here!

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:21.000
Tomorrow we'll be blasting off into space.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:25.290
This might be the last time we look up at the stars like this!

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:27.710
Don't jinx us!

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:28.630
Yeah, yeah!

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.310
We're not going so we can die.

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.330
That's right! It's so we can live!

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.260
So we can live...

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:43.090
Let's come back alive.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.100
No matter what happens, let's live through it.

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:55.880
No! I'm going too!

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:57.340
Sorry.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:01.860
But from the start, we'd decided you'd stay behind, Adam.

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:03.230
Why?

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.700
Even though I'm your friend...

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.350
That's not the problem.

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:11.330
Even if this plan is successful, there's no guarantee we'll make it back safely.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.490
That's why I want to help you!

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:16.050
Don't be ridiculous!

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:19.280
We want to leave as many people behind as we can!

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:26.100
Adam, stay behind with Tako and protect this planet's animals and environment.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:28.540
We all decided this.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.420
No! I'm going too!

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:31.630
Don't be so selfish!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.680
You're staying behind, Adam. For this planet's future!

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:50.850
Everyone...

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:52.730
...good luck.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:01.200
Louis...

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:03.490
...I'm going so we can live.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.650
Heat shield, standby!

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:16.010
Perform final checks!

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:17.890
Energy system!

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.750
External supply line disconnected.

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.250
Generator operating.

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:26.170
Flow to the gravity control system nominal.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.160
Gravity control unit!

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:31.050
Energy supply nominal.

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:34.610
Gluon controller and Exotic controller nominal.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:36.450
Tensor variation rate: 0.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:37.920
Flight plan!

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.690
No change in gravity storm's course.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:43.800
Ship's initial parameter check finished.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.650
Ship's course recalculations finished.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:48.510
No change in parameters.

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:51.890
Flight plan load successful. No system problems.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:53.780
Cockpit condition!

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:56.780
Airtight seal okay. Temperature: 23ﾂｰC.

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:58.910
Oxygen/Nitrogen ratio nominal.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:01.010
Ship's internal gravity: 1.0G.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.230
Airflow nominal.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:03.730
Communications system!

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:05.740
Voice check okay.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:06.900
Gain okay.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:08.480
Preparations finished!

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:10.160
Start countdown!

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.130
Thirty... Twenty-nine... Twenty-eight...

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:13.950
Gravity control unit operational!

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.050
...Twenty-seven... Twenty-six... Twenty-five...

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:17.060
Output increasing.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:17.440
...Twenty-four... Twenty-three... Twenty-two...

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:19.580
Tensor variation rate: 3%.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:20.550
...Twenty-four... Twenty-three... Twenty-two...

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:23.590
...Twenty-one... Twenty... Nineteen...

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.630
...Eighteen... Seventeen... Sixteen...

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.190
...Fifteen... Fourteen... Thirteen...

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:33.150
...Twelve... Eleven... Ten...

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.940
Seventeen... Sixteen... Fifteen...

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:55.200
...Fourteen... Thirteen... Twelve...

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:58.650
...Eleven... Ten... Nine...

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:01.690
...Eight... Seven... Six...

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:04.500
...Five... Four... Three...

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:06.790
...Two... One...

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:07.880
Liftoff!

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:02.960
Gravity control unit output within 0.1%.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:04.060
Well within tolerances.

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:05.520
Flight okay.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:08.250
Automatic shutoff system to manual.

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:16.840
Three minutes since launch.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.450
On course to enter the gravity storm.

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:27.330
Cut off energy flow to communications unit.

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:28.430
Roger!

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:37.580
Charge energy to the gravity control unit for destroying the gravity storm!

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:38.700
Roger!

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:41.510
Calculate adjustments to course to gravity storm.

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:44.930
Calculations okay. Flight plan modifications finished.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.310
Thruster burn, standby!

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.690
Standing by.

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:51.150
Ready for alignment!

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:52.280
Burn!

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:59.590
No change in gravity storm's course.

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:03.870
Return course to planet following release of gravity control unit also confirmed.

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:05.980
Energy output stable.

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:09.340
Gravity control system charge is okay.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:12.020
Ship's systems are all green.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:16.350
Roger. Halt energy supply to thruster unit!

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:17.400
Roger.

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:25.240
We'll let inertia take us the rest of the way.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:29.510
Activating autopilot. Everyone, well done!

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:33.530
We just switched over to autopilot.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.190
It's been a success so far.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:37.540
They did it!

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:42.080
Roger! Keep it up just like that!

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:42.920
Aye-aye!

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.430
It's a very pretty planet.

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.810
We're protecting this planet.

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.500
The gravity storm...

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:13.540
The gravity storm has come into view!

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:18.150
The gravity storm's energy is increasing.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.140
Putting it on the monitor!

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:26.590
Can we really destroy that thing?

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.100
The calculations said we could.

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:30.080
Yeah...

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:33.790
But the energy level's increased more'n we thought.

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:38.490
If we used the energy from the gravity storm itself,

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.650
we could use it to make the inverse gravitational field, right?

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:46.280
If the ship's gravity control unit has the strength to do it...

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:50.550
Energy supply to the thruster unit has been restored!

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:52.130
What?

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:54.110
Send the numbers over here.

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:54.720
Roger!

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.980
What does this mean?

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:02.900
It can't be!

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:07.910
The thrusters are operating!

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.230
Our course has changed!

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:22.090
What happened?

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:23.320
Kaoru, do you know?

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:25.650
The safety program is running!

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:27.710
Why?

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:28.610
It's Survive!

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:34.460
Survive, what's the meaning of this?

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:40.620
I can't switch from autopilot back to manual pilot!

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:42.410
Survive!

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:44.920
At this rate we'll go back to the planet!

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:47.930
If we don't fix our course, we won't make it!

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:51.000
Damn Survive! We came all this way for him to backstab us?

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.610
But why?

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:56.180
I'll go ask.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:57.920
Everyone, stand by.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.950
Why did you stop the space ship?

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:15.390
Tell me the reason!

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:20.660
The gravity storm's energy has increased beyond predictions.

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:28.400
It is impossible for the gravity control unit on this space ship to destroy it.

00:17:29.030 --> 00:17:31.310
We won't know that if we don't try!

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:35.660
I know the most about this space ship.

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:39.410
What my data says is impossible is definitely impossible.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.440
We have no choice but to avoid it.

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:42.450
Avoid it?

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:48.300
Yes. If we continue as we are, I will be destroyed along with the gravity control unit.

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:49.800
What do we do after we avoid it?

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:54.490
My primary duty is to protect the environment of the planet.

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:57.410
But the gravity storm is definitely coming.

00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:00.170
When that happens, what will you do?

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:03.720
My duty is to pro...

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:08.100
If we return to the planet without doing anything, the planet will definitely be destroyed.

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:11.850
That should also be clear from your data.

00:18:13.390 --> 00:18:16.850
So you should take a chance on any possibility, however small it may be.

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:20.510
I have my duty...

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:22.010
Let's try it!

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:25.150
If you don't have the courage to do it, then absorb me...

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:27.040
Absorb?

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:30.530
Yes. You mentioned it before, right?

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:35.700
That if you absorbed me, you might be able to gain my mysterious power.

00:18:36.410 --> 00:18:37.690
So try it out!

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:43.800
It may have some effect on your body. Are you okay with that?

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:46.200
Yes.

00:18:47.030 --> 00:18:52.650
You may even cease to exist as a person. Are you okay with that?

00:18:57.000 --> 00:19:00.790
If we give up, we and this planet can do nothing but wait for death.

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:03.450
I'll never give up!

00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:07.650
Very well!

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:48.490
I see...

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:56.930
Your power is not a negative power born from hatred and anger.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:01.420
It is the desire to save your friends, your bonds with them,

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:09.190
and the strong desire to live that give the power to live to all living things.

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:11.700
The power to live.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:12.970
Yes.

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:16.970
Perhaps you are a new breed of person.

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:19.460
New breed?

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:21.860
I am?

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:25.440
No, I think it is the opposite.

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:27.110
The opposite?

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:32.700
The very first life was surely born from the strong desire to live.

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:39.640
So even the moment they are born, people are filled with the desire to live.

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:45.860
So that strong desire to live manifested itself?

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:49.990
But as a machine, I do not have that desire.

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:56.000
But Survive, have you thought about the meaning of your name?

00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:58.000
My name?

00:20:58.690 --> 00:20:59.630
Yes.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.630
Your name, "Survive,"

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:05.000
...means, "to go on living."

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:09.190
I... go on living...

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:13.280
So survive! No matter what hardships you may face!

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:20.600
Control is back to manual!

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:23.890
Everyone, can you hear me?

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:24.540
Luna!

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:26.930
Did you persuade Survive?

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:28.240
Yes, Kaoru.

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:30.860
Keep heading for the gravity storm.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:32.060
Very well.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:33.980
Restart the operation!

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:36.650
Recalculate entry and return courses!

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:49.840
On course for entry.

00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:51.230
Return course okay too!

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:55.160
At this rate, we'll enter the gravity storm in one hundred and twenty minutes.

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:56.890
Finally...

00:21:57.450 --> 00:21:59.660
Luna, aren't you coming back here?

00:22:00.190 --> 00:22:01.280
I'm...

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:03.790
...with Survive.

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.410
'With'? Why?

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:07.710
I can't come back right now.

00:22:08.330 --> 00:22:10.160
Luna, what do you mean?

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:14.330
Damn it!

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:17.180
We were almost at the release point!

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.510
The energy level of the gravity storm is increasing!

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:23.510
It's only a little further to the release point!

00:22:23.740 --> 00:22:27.450
Activate the gravity control system and contradict the abnormal gravity!

00:22:28.090 --> 00:22:28.730
Roger!

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:02.750
Menori...

00:23:03.450 --> 00:23:05.210
...Sharla, Howard...

00:23:06.300 --> 00:23:06.800
...Bell...

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:09.170
...Chako, Shingo...

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:10.910
...Kaoru...

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:13.050
...Adam, Tako...

00:23:14.100 --> 00:23:16.840
I'm really glad I met all of you.

00:23:17.510 --> 00:23:21.530
I'll never forget the time I spent on this planet.

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:24.560
Forever, no matter what happens.

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:28.310
Next time: To where everyone is.
